## Chapter 05: Increment and Decrement

![Illustration of prefix, postfix, and nullish coalescing](assets/images/javascript-increment-decrement.svg)

The increment and decrement lessons show how `++` and `--` update a variable, and why prefix and postfix expressions can produce different values during the same operation. The final lesson introduces `??`, which uses a fallback only when the left side is `null` or `undefined`.

Lessons: [`38_ID_OP.js`](05_chapter_JS_Incre_Decre_OP/38_ID_OP.js), [`39_ID.js`](05_chapter_JS_Incre_Decre_OP/39_ID.js), [`40_IQ.js`](05_chapter_JS_Incre_Decre_OP/40_IQ.js), [`41_IQ.js`](05_chapter_JS_Incre_Decre_OP/41_IQ.js), [`42_IQ.js`](05_chapter_JS_Incre_Decre_OP/42_IQ.js), [`43_Decre.js`](05_chapter_JS_Incre_Decre_OP/43_Decre.js), [`44_JS.js`](05_chapter_JS_Incre_Decre_OP/44_JS.js), and [`45.Nullish.js`](05_chapter_JS_Incre_Decre_OP/45.Nullish.js).

